          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em KK-theory
            is a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivariant+cohomology+theory"}> bivariant
            ” joint generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-homology"} K-homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            %em KK-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK(A,B)
            is a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+bimodules"} Hilbert bimodules
            equipped with an additional left weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+module"} Fredholm module
            structure. These KK-groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK(A,B)
            behave in the first argument as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-homology"} K-homology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and in the second as
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-cohomology"} K-cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            Abstractly, KK-theory is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            which is the split-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact
            and
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            at the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+operators"} compact operators
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+module"} Fredolm
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+bimodules"} Hilbert bimodules
            as above is rooted in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-theory"} E-theory
          %p
            Due to this joint root in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            and (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"}> noncommutative
            )
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+stable+homotopy+theory"}> noncommutative stable homotopy theory
            ”), KK-theory is a natural home of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+operators"} elliptic operators
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            as well as for their generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            situations, to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
            and generally to
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            = succeed ")" do
