                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-theory"} E-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} …
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            KK-theory was introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennady+Kasparov"} Gennady Kasparov
            in
          %ul
            %li#Kasparov80
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennady+Kasparov"}> Gennady Kasparov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The operator
                  = succeed "-functor" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\ast}
              %strong 44
              (1980), no. 3, 571-636, 719,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=582160"} MR81m:58075
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.zentralblatt-math.org/zmath/search/?an=Zbl%200464.46054%7CZbl%200448.46051"} Zbl
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/archive.phtml?wshow=paper&jrnid=im&paperid=1739&option_lang=eng"} abstract
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1070%2FIM1981v016n03ABEH001320"} english doi
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=im&paperid=1739&volume=44&year=1980&issue=3&fpage=571&what=fullt&option_lang=eng"} pdf
          %p
            prompted by the advances in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown-Douglas-Fillmore+theory"} Brown-Douglas-Fillmore theory
          %p Some streamlining of the definitions appeared in
          %ul
            %li#Skandalis84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Skandalis"}> Georges Skandalis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Some remarks on Kasparov theory
          %p A textbook account is in
          %ul
            %li#Blackadar99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Blackadar"}> Bruce Blackadar
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-Theory+for+Operator+Algebras"} K-Theory for Operator Algebras
          %p Introductions and surveys include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gennady+Kasparov"}> Gennady Kasparov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Operator K-theory and its applications: elliptic operators, group representations, higher signatures
                    = succeed "-extensions" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Higson"}> Nigel Higson
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em A primer on KK-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.psu.edu/higson/math/Papers_files/Higson%20-%201990%20-%20A%20primer%20on%20KK-theory.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Skandalis"}> Georges Skandalis
                ,
                %em Kasparov’s bivariant K-theory and applications
                Exposition. Math. 9, 193–250 (1991) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.vanderbilt.edu/~bisch/ncgoa08/talks/skandalis2.pdf"}> pdf slides
                )
            %li#Introduction
              %p
                %em> Introduction to KK-theory and E-theory
                , Lecture notes (Lisbon 2009) (
                %a{:href => "http://oaa.ist.utl.pt/files/cursos/courseD_Lecture4_KK_and_E1.pdf"}> pdf slides
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+Meyer"} R. Meyer
                (notes taken by S. Hong),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em KK-theory and Baum-Connes conjecture
                %em Summer school on operator algebras and noncommutative geometry
                (June 2010) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.pims.math.ca/files/EM_%20KK-theory_BC_Conjecture.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Meyer06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+Meyer"}> R. Meyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em How analysis and topology interact in bivariant K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://mate.dm.uba.ar/~gcorti/article.pdf"} pdf
          %p On an approach using quasi-homomorphisms:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Cuntz"}> Joachim Cuntz
              , James Gabe.
              %em Generalized homomorphisms and KK with extra structure
              (2024). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.06840"}> arXiv:2404.06840
              ).
          %h3#excision Excision
          %p Excision for KK-theory is further studied in
          %ul
            %li#CuntzSkandalis86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Cuntz"}> Joachim Cuntz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Skandalis"} Georges Skandalis
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mapping cones and exact sequences in KK-theory
            %li#Skandalis88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Skandalis"}> Georges Skandalis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Une notion de nuclearité en K-theorie
          %h3#in_category_theory_and_homotopy_theory In Category theory and Homotopy theory
          %p
            KK-theory is naturally understood in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+properties"} universal properties
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p
            That
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK(A,B)
            is naturally thought of as a collection of “generalized
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Cuntz"}> Joachim Cuntz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Generalized Homomorphisms Between
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0072109"} 10.1007/BFb0072109
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Cuntz"}> Joachim Cuntz
                ,
                %em
                  K-theory and C
                  %em -algebras,_ Springer Lecture Notes in Mathematics, 1046 (1984), 55-79.
          %p
            That under the Kasparov product these are indeed the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            was first observed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Higson"}> Nigel Higson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A characterization of KK-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.pjm/1102699804"} EUCLID
          %p
            where moreover this category is realized as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
            additive and split exact “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"}> localization
            ” of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg
            at the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+operators"} compact operators
          %p
            The generalization of this statement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            KK-theory is in
          %ul
            %li#Thomsen98
              Klaus Thomsen,
              %em The universal property of equivariant KK-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0249/"}> K-theory preprint
              )
          %p
            Characterization of KK-theory as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/satellites"} satellites
            of a functor is in
          %ul
            %li#Inassaridze
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hvedri+Inassaridze"}> Hvedri Inassaridze
              ,
              %em Universal property of Kasparov bivariant K-theory
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/InassaridzeOnKK.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bielefeld.de/~bak/kasp.ps"} ps
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            structure for KK-theory is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Meyer
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"}> Ralf Meyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical aspects of bivariant K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702145"} arXiv:math/0702145
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"}> Ralf Meyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryszard+Nest"} Ryszard Nest
                %em Homological algebra in bivariant K-theory and other triangulated categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702146"}> arXiv:math/0702146
                )
            %li#Meyer
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"}> Ralf Meyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em KK-theory as a triangulated category
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/echters/Focused-Semester/lecturenotes/Meyer_--_KK-theory_as_a_triangulated_category.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            realization of KK-theory is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#JoachimJohnson07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"}> Michael Joachim
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Johnson"} Mark Johnson
              %em Realizing Kasparov’s KK-theory groups as the homotopy classes of maps of a Quillen model category
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.1971"}> arXiv:0705.1971
              )
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            which unifies the above homotopical pictures is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Uuye10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Otgonbayar+Uuye"}> Otgonbayar Uuye
              ,
              %em
                Homotopy theory for
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.2926"}> arXiv:1011.2926
              )
          %p
            More on this is at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+structure+on+C%2A-algebras"} homotopical structure on C*-algebras
          %p
            Further discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-theory"} E-theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Martin Grensing,
                %em Noncommutative stable homotopy theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1302.4751"}> arXiv:1302.4751
                )
            %li#Mahanta11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdhayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdhayan Mahanta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Higher nonunital Quillen
                    = succeed "-theory," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi K
                            %mo ′
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
                    = succeed "-duality" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝕋
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/snigdhayan.mahanta/papers/KQ.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Refinement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            to cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BunkeJoachimStolz03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"} Michael Joachim
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephan+Stolz"} Stephan Stolz
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Classifying spaces and spectra representing the K-theory of a graded
                  = succeed "-algebra" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %p
            This construction is functorial (only) for
            %em essential
            = succeed "-homomorphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
          %h3#AsHomotopyOfStableInfinityCategoryReferences
            As the homotopy category of a stable
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            A refinement of the KK-category to a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
          %ul
            %li#JoachimStolz09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"}> Michael Joachim
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephan+Stolz"} Stephan Stolz
              %em
                An enrichment of
                = succeed "-theory" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi KK
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK
              Münster J. of Math. 2 (2009), 143–182 (
              %a{:href => "http://www3.nd.edu/~stolz/KKenrich.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            and the generalization of this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            over geometrically discrete groupoids is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Mitchener07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Mitchener"}> Paul Mitchener
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi KK
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK
                \-theory spectra for
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.2152"}> arXiv:0711.2152
              )
          %p but this construction is stated to be mistaken on p. 3 of
          %ul
            %li#DEKM11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Dell%27Ambrogio"}> Ivo Dell'Ambrogio
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"} Heath Emerson
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tamaz+Kandelaki"} Tamaz Kandelaki
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"} Ralf Meyer
              %em A functorial equivariant K-theory spectrum and an equivariant Lefschetz formula
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.3441"}> arXiv:1104.3441
              )
          %p
            This article in turn considers a variant of the construction in (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeJoachimStolz03"}> Bunke-Joachim-Stolz 03
            ) which gives operator K-theory spectra that are functorial for general
            = succeed "-homomorphisms." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
          %p
            Observations relating to a genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            structure maybe at least of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-theory"} E-theory
            are in
          %ul
            %li#Mahanta12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdhayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdhayan Mahanta
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Noncommutative stable homotopy and semigroup
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.6576"} arXiv:1211.6576
          %p
            A complete realization of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"}> equivariant
            , even) KK-theory as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                stable
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li#BunkeEngelLand21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Engel"} Alexander Engel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Land"} Markus Land
              %em
                A stable
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.13372"} arXiv:2102.13372
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %h3#in_the_context_of_the_novikov_conjecture In the context of the Novikov conjecture
          %ul
            %li#Rosenberg80
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"}> Jonathan Rosenberg
              ,
              %em
                Group C
                %em -algebras and Topological Invariants_ , Proc. Conf. in Neptun, Romania, 1980, Pitman (London, 1985)
          %h3#in_the_context_of_the_atiyahsinger_index_theorem In the context of the Atiyah-Singer index theorem
          %p
            The classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Singer+index+theorem"} Atiyah-Singer index theorem
            is reviewed in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            (with some hints towards KK-theory) in
          %ul
            %li#HigsonRoe
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Higson"}> Nigel Higson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Roe"} John Roe
              %em Lectures on operator K-theory and the Atiyah-Singer Index Theorem
              (2004) (
              %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/rognes/higson/Book.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Generalization to the relative case in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+operators"} elliptic operators
            on
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+C%2A-module"} Hilbert C*-module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Jody Trout,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Asymptotic Morphisms and Elliptic Operators over
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9906098"} arXiv:math/9906098
          %h3#for_convolution_algebras_and_in_geometric_quantization For convolution algebras and In geometric quantization
          %p
            Discussion of KK-theory with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+of+a+C-star+algebra"} C-star representations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution algebras
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+by+push-forward"} by push-forward
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"}> Klaas Landsman
                ,
                %em Quantization as a functor
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0107023"}> arXiv:math-ph/0107023
                )
            %li#Landsman03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"}> Klaas Landsman
                ,
                %em Functorial quantization and the Guillemin-Sternberg conjecture
                , Proc. Bialowieza 2002 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0307059"}> arXiv:math-ph/0307059
                )
            %li#Bos07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rogier+Bos"}> Rogier Bos
                ,
                %em Groupoids in geometric quantization
                PhD Thesis (2007) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ist.utl.pt/~rbos/ProefschriftA4.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p with a summary/exposition in
          %ul
            %li#Landsman10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"}> Klaas Landsman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Functoriality of quantization: a KK-theoretic approach
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.academia.edu/1992202/Functoriality_of_quantization_a_KK-theoretic_approach"} web
          %p
            See also the related references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guillemin-Sternberg+geometric+quantization+conjecture"} Guillemin-Sternberg geometric quantization conjecture
          %p
            The KK-theory of twisted convolution algebras and its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#TXLG
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Tu"}> Jean-Louis Tu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Camille+Laurent-Gengoux"} Camille Laurent-Gengoux
              %em Twisted K-theory of differentiable stacks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0306138"}> arXiv:math/0306138
              )
          %p
            Discussion of groupoid 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            and their effect on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+algebra"} groupoid algebra
            KK-theory is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Bram Mesland,
              %em Groupoid cocycles and K-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.3677"}> arXiv:1005.3677
              )
          %h3#ReferencesInTermsOfCorrespondences In terms of correspondences/spans
          %h4#for_plain_kktheory For plain KK-theory
          %p
            KK-classes between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            are described in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            manifolds carrying a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            in section 3 of
          %ul
            %li#ConnesSkandalis84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Skandalis"} Georges Skandalis
              = succeed "," do
                %em The longitudinal index theorem for foliations
              %strong 20
              6, 1139-1183 (1984) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/docs/longitudinal.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            This generalizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baum-Douglas+geometric+cycles"} Baum-Douglas geometric cycles
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-homology"} K-homology
            to KK-theory.
          %p
            A further generalization of this, where one algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(Y)
            is generalized to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(Y) \otimes A
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a unital separable
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %ul
            %li#BlockWeinberger99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Block"}> Jonathan Block
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shmuel+Weinberger"} Shmuel Weinberger
              = succeed "," do
                %em Arithmetic manifolds of positive scalar curvature
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.30.297"} web
          %p In section 5 of
          %ul
            %li#BrodzkiMathaiRosenbergSzabo07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacek+Brodzki"}> Jacek Brodzki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"} Varghese Mathai
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative correspondences, duality and D-branes in bivariant K-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2648"} arXiv:0708.2648
          %p
            this is reviewed and then a characterization in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-spans"} co-spans
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            is given. This version is effectively a restatement of
            %a{:href => "#RelationToHomotopyClassesOfStarHomomorphisms"} the characterization by Cuntz
            as reproduced in (
            %a{:href => "#Blackadar99"}> Blackadar 99, corollary 17.8.4
            ).
          %p
            For similar structures see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motive"} motive
            in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "motive#RelationToKKTheory"} Relation to bivariant K-theory
          %p A ‘generators and relations’ description of KK-theory in terms of spans is given in
          %ul
            %li
              Bernhard Burgstaller,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The generators and relations picture of KK-theory
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1602.03034"} 1602.03034
          %h4#ReferencesCorrespondencesEquivariant For equivariant KK-theory
          %p
            Generalization of such
            = succeed "-presentation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+KK-theory"} equivariant KK-theory
            (and hence, by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Julg+theorem"} Green-Julg theorem
            essentially to KK-theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+algebras"} groupoid algebras
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoids"} action groupoids
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+groups"} compact topological groups
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"} Ralf Meyer
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bivariant K-theory via correspondences
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4949"} arXiv:0812.4949
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li#EmersonMeyer09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"} Ralf Meyer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant embedding theorems and topological index maps
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.1465"} arXiv:0908.1465
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"} Ralf Meyer
                %em Dualities in equivariant Kasparov theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.0025"}> arXiv:0711.0025
                )
          %p based on technical aspects of the construction of pushforward along and comoposition of equivariant correspondences in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Baum"}> Paul Baum
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Block"} Jonathan Block
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Equivariant bicycles on singular spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.upenn.edu/~blockj/papers/BlockEquivariantbi.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"} Ralf Meyer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant embedding theorems and topological index maps
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.1465"} arXiv:0908.1465
          %p Further developments of this are in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
                ,
                %em Duality, correspondences and the Lefschetz map in equivariant KK-theory: a survey
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0904.4744"}> arXiv:0904.4744
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
                , Robert Yuncken,
                %em Equivariant correspondences and the Borel-Bott-Weil theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.1153"}> arXiv:0905.1153
                )
          %h3#RelationToMotives Relation to motives and algebraic KK-theory
          %p
            The general analogy between KK-cocycles and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives"} motives
            is noted explicitly in
          %ul
            %li#ConnesConsaniMarcolli05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                , Caterina Consani,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"} Matilde Marcolli
                %em Noncommutative geometry and motives: the thermodynamics of endomotives
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0512138"}> arXiv:math/0512138
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"} Matilde Marcolli
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry%2C+Quantum+Fields+and+Motives"} Noncommutative Geometry, Quantum Fields and Motives
          %p
            and also very briefly in (
            %a{:href => "#Meyer06"}> Meyer 06
            ).
          %p
            A relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            and bivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guillermo+Corti%C3%B1as"}> Guillermo Cortiñas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Thom"} Andreas Thom
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bivariant algebraic K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0603531"} arXiv:math/0603531
            %li#Mahanta09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdahayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdahayan Mahanta
                ,
                %em
                  Noncommutative correspondence categories, simplicial sets and pro
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.5400"}> arXiv:0906.5400
                )
            %li#Mahanta11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdahayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdahayan Mahanta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Higher nonunital Quillen
                    = succeed "-theory," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi K
                            %mo ′
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
                    = succeed "-duality" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝕋
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/snigdhayan.mahanta/papers/KQ.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GarkushaPanin11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigory+Garkusha"}> Grigory Garkusha
                , Ivan Panin,
                %em K-motives of algebraic varieties
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.0375"}> arXiv:1108.0375
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigory+Garkusha"}> Grigory Garkusha
                ,
                %em Algebraic Kasparov K-theory. II
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.0178"}> arXiv:1206.0178
                )
          %p For a collection of literature see also paragraph 1.5 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gon%C3%A7alo+Tabuada"} Gonçalo Tabuada
              %em A universal characterization of higher algebraic K-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.2282"}> arXiv:1001.2282
              )
          %p
            (in the context of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+motives"} noncommutative motives
          %p In
          %ul
            %li#Mahanta13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdhayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdhayan Mahanta
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Higher nonunital Quillen
                  = succeed "-theory," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/snigdhayan.mahanta/papers/KQ.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/snigdhayan.mahanta/papers/KKTD.pdf"} talk notes
          %p
            it is shown that there is a universal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi NCC
                    %mi dg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK \longrightarrow NCC_{dg}
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            to the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+motives"} noncommutative motives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-categories"} dg-categories
            and dg-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            up to homotopy between them. This is given by sending a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+complexes"} perfect complexes
            of (the unitalization of) its underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives+in+physics"} motives in physics
          %h3#in_dbrane_theory In D-brane theory
          %p
            KK-theory also describes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charges"} charges
            and sources in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            theory.
          %p A review is in
          %ul
            %li#Szabo
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"}> Richard Szabo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-branes and bivariant K-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.3029"} arXiv:0809.3029
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacek+Brodzki"}> Jacek Brodzki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"} Varghese Mathai
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %p
                %em> D-Branes, RR-Fields and Duality on Noncommutative Manifolds
                , Commun. Math. Phys.
                %strong 277
                (2008) 643-706 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0607020"}> arXiv:hep-th/0607020
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-007-0396-y"} doi:10.1007/s00220-007-0396-y
              %p
                %em> Noncommutative correspondences, duality and D-branes in bivariant K-theory
                , Adv. Theor. Math. Phys.13:497-552,2009 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2648"}> arXiv:0708.2648
                )
              %p
                %em> D-branes, KK-theory and duality on noncommutative spaces
                , J. Phys. Conf. Ser. 103:012004,2008 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.2128"}> arXiv:0709.2128
                )
          %h3#smooth_refinement_and_spectral_triples Smooth refinement and spectral triples
          %p
            Discussion of KK-theory for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bram+Mesland"}> Bram Mesland
              ,
              %em Spectral triples and KK-theory: A survey
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3802"}> arXiv:1304.3802
              )
        .revisedby
          %p
            Last revised on September  8, 2025 at 13:08:46.
